BT 1 0 0 1 0 86 Tm /F3+0 10 Tf 12 TL (\(A-D\) Selected paired comparisons of outcome rates during pair-specific mono-detection and co-detection: all-age LRTI \(A\), all-age) Tj T* (hospital admission \(B\), death in children younger than 5 years \(C\), and LRTI in adults older than 60 years \(D\). Reference groups are) Tj T* (defined as in figure 2. Points represent eligible pairs, grey lines connect the two rates for each pair, and boxplots show medians and) Tj T* (interquartile ranges. P values are from two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank tests. \(E-I\) Five eligible pairs with the highest) Tj T* (co-detection-associated LRTI, hospital-admission, ICU-admission, and death rates in children younger than 5 years \(E\), those aged) Tj T* (5\00117 years \(F\), adults aged 18-60 years \(G\), adults older than 60 years \(H\), and unknown age \(I\). Rates use outcome-known) Tj T* (co-detection windows; numbers in parentheses indicate the total number of co-detection windows for each pathogen pair, whereas) Tj T* (outcome rates were calculated among windows with known status for the corresponding outcome.) Tj T* ET
